Subject: Fills the register PIC and reads it inline on the hot named-property path

What this does
  Fills the register PIC and reads it inline on the hot named-property path.

Why we need it
  The register backend had a per-function PIC with no owner, no fill and no hit, so every named read paid the generic engine lookup.

What it adds
  `regvm_pic_fill` fills one shape per site for a plain, non-exotic receiver with a counted-ref, hashed shape, a direct-prototype or own data property, no `JS_PROP_LENGTH` and no lazy slot, with an eight-miss megamorphic cutoff; `regvm_get_field_ic` keeps the engine lookup and fills from it; `regvm_own_read_hit` reads `f->pic`/`pic` with one shape compare and a kind test, inlined into `regvm_t_get_field`/`_get_field2`/`_get_local_field_0` and the monolith; the frame re-points its base after the lazy allocation.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
